  "query_preview": "..\n\nThe rest of today through Sunday..\n\nUpper level ridging will continue to bring warm and mostly dry\nconditions to the region through the work week.\n\nA shortwave moves through the area Tuesday, bringing a low chance\n(10-30%) for light showers and will keep highs in the 50s to low\n60s. Ahead of the shortwave, the pressure gradient tightens, \nincreasing winds over the western foothills. This will bring gusts\nof 20 to 40 mph over the Livingston to Nye area tonight. Then, as\nthe shortwave moves through, winds will increase from west to \neast Tuesday morning into afternoon. Currently, the chance for \nexceeding 50 mph is 25% at Livingston, 40% at Big Timber, and 65% \nfor Harlowton. Over the plains, gusts of 25 to 35 mph will be \ncommon, and a few locations may see a stray gust into the low 40s \nmph.\n\nThrough the end of the work week, upper level ridging builds over\nthe region, keeping conditions dry and warm. Normal highs for \nthis time of year are in the mid to upper 40s. By Thursday, highs \nwill be in the 60s to near 70, around 15 to 25 degrees above \nnormal.\n\nFor the weekend, ensembles and cluster analysis show lower \nheights building into the region as upper troughing gradually \npushes inland over the western US. This will help break down the\nridge and may allow for cooler and more unsettled weather to move\nin late this weekend/early next week. Archer",
